  "description_short": "Contemporary dining in George's Outeniqua Village with fresh, seasonal flavors and a relaxed atmosphere.",
  "description_long": "Tucked into Outeniqua Village on the edge of George, Cula Restaurant has built a loyal following with its contemporary approach to fresh, seasonal cooking. The space feels modern and welcoming, with clean lines and comfortable seating that works equally well for a quick business lunch or a leisurely dinner with friends.\n\nThe menu changes with the seasons but consistently delivers well-executed dishes that balance familiar comfort with creative touches. Expect quality steaks, fresh line fish, and thoughtful vegetarian options, all plated with care. The kitchen doesn't overcomplicate things – they let good ingredients speak for themselves. Portions are generous without being overwhelming, and the wine list offers solid local choices at fair prices.\n\nThe location on Saint George's Road makes it easily accessible whether you're staying in George or passing through on the Garden Route. Service is attentive without hovering, and the atmosphere strikes a nice balance between casual and polished. It's the kind of place that works for everything from a family meal to a celebration dinner, and regulars keep coming back for consistently good food in a space that feels both fresh and familiar.",
